00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,825
- Me?
- Probably just that debt collector again.

250
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:35,411
You know it's not our job
to deal with those kinds of calls.

251
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:38,747
Well, I don't think it's a doctor's job,
either, you know?

252
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:42,459
And what if it's an actual emergency, huh?

253
00:16:44,461 --> 00:16:46,130
Katsushika Medical University Hospital.

254
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,257
<i>I'm sorry to call so late.</i>

255
00:16:48,757 --> 00:16:51,218
<i>This is Makihara from Nagomi Bank.</i>

256
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:53,804
<i>Is Dr. Numata available?</i>

257
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:59,184
E806
VACANT

258
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:06,650
Hey, how many times do I have to tell you,
no breaks in the inpatient ward.

259
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:08,027
- What? Ow!
- Huh?

260
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:10,487
- What is it?
- I'm not your assistant.

261
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:13,323
It's Makihara
from that whatchamacallit bank.

262
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,826
Why don't you tell him I'm not here?

263
00:17:15,909 --> 00:17:17,494
You're bothering everyone.

264
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:25,711
Oh, hello, Mr. Makihara.

265
00:17:25,794 --> 00:17:28,380
This is Numata. Yes, yes, I'm sorry.

266
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:31,216
<i>I'm so sorry to interrupt.</i>
<i>I know you're busy.</i>

267
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,886
<i>I'm calling about the outstanding debt</i>
<i>from Change the World.</i>

268
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:37,056
<i>- The business you co-manage.</i>
- Oh no, listen, I… I don't co-manage it.

269
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:38,932
I don't even know why my name's on it.

270
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:41,602
<i>The payment deadline</i>
<i>is at the end of the month.</i>

271
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:45,564
- <i>I was planning to come by your hospital--</i>
- Oh, sorry, I have a surgery to perform!

272
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:46,690
I'll call you back later.

273
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,443
- What?
- We have an emergency.

274
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:57,034
Comatose at a party?
Must be alcohol poisoning.

275
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,369
Actually, the patient
hadn't been drinking.

276
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:01,872
The hotel sent someone over
with her belongings.

277
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:03,749
You should talk to her directly.

278
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:04,917
No alcohol…

279
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:07,961
Wait, did she get injections?

280
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:12,174
Yes. She had a few shots, and suddenly
she started drifting in and out.

281
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,843
You said she was at a party.
How did she get injections?

282
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:17,346
We're going to run a CT scan now.

283
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:20,015
Let's find out the source of your pain.

284
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:23,268
It might be
a little uncomfortable, but hang in there.

285
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:25,395
She's a natural beauty influencer.

286
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:27,481
Dr. Tojo is a huge fan of hers.

287
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:30,400
Yeah, he never misses her live streams.

288
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:35,072
A large abscess pressing on the silicone.

289
00:18:35,155 --> 00:18:37,199
- And some findings indicate a tumor.
- What?

290
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:39,493
Silicone?

291
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:42,079
She's not a natural beauty after all.

292
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:43,455
- Huh?
- Huh.

293
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:46,041
Her yearbook photo was adorable, though.

294
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,376
I know, right?

295
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:49,294
The patient will be here soon.

296
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:50,879
- You know her?
- No way.

297
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,340
- Hey!
- Huh? Uh…

298
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:55,217
Ms. Kokubun, the pain you're feeling

299
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:57,803
is coming from an abscess
in your left breast.

300
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:59,888
It's pressing against the implant.

301
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:02,808
So we are going to need
to remove the silicone before--

302
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:05,602
- Doctor!
- Yes?

303
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:09,565
- Don't take the silicone out.
- That's your concern?

304
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,819
So the natural beauty thing was a lie.

305
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:16,280
That's her concern. Let's begin. Go ahead.

306
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,407
Okay, I'm gonna put a mask on you.

307
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,909
- We're starting.
- You're gonna feel drowsy.

308
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:30,836
<i>Hm? She concealed her self-harm scars.</i>

309
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:33,005
Checking now.

310
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:37,801
<i>She had surgery only a week ago.</i>

311
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:40,846
<i>She's crazy to get Botox</i>
<i>so soon after surgery.</i>

312
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:44,099
<i>Her eyes, nose, and jaw</i>
<i>have all been operated on.</i>

313
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:46,476
<i>It's harder to find a natural part of her.</i>

314
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:47,936
- Here.
- Right.

315
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:49,730
Let's proceed.

316
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,524
MOM

317
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:57,863
Mom, hi.

318
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:01,909
<i>Seriously, why didn't you</i>
<i>pick up sooner? What's going on?</i>

319
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:04,077
I'm still on shift.

320
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:06,038
I'm sorry. I have to go.

321
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:09,541
<i>Wait! They're saying</i>
<i>your dad might not make it past next week.</i>

322
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:11,710
<i>Listen, Yoshiko.</i>

323
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:14,713
<i>I can't do this alone anymore.</i>

324
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:17,090
<i>And I can't keep the shop closed forever.</i>

325
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:19,092
Sorry, I'm still at work, Mom.

326
00:20:19,176 --> 00:20:20,385
<i>Wait, wait!</i>

327
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:28,685
So, does being an influencer

328
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:32,105
require you to put foreign materials
in your body while you heal?

329
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:38,612
Hm.

330
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:41,698
So, Dr. Tojo,
now that you've met her in person,

331
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:42,866
what do you think?

332
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:44,159
Not funny.

333
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,245
This is what you were so excited about.

334
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:47,287
Focus.

335
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:48,372
Hm, looks good.

336
00:20:48,872 --> 00:20:50,332
- Irrigation.
- Ready.

337
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:03,512
Inhale.

338
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:06,932
And exhale.

339
00:21:11,186 --> 00:21:12,479
Connect to your core.

340
00:21:13,188 --> 00:21:14,022
Here.

341
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,107
Thanks.

342
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:18,568
Oh. I made your rice portion smaller
since you had champagne last night.

343
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:21,697
That's not nice.

344
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:25,200
- Okay, let's have our meal.
- Let's have our meal.

345
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:52,853
GREAT PARTY LAST NIGHT.
LET ME THANK YOU WITH DINNER?

346
00:21:52,936 --> 00:21:55,522
Have you heard anything about Kanabun?

347
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:57,774
I just talked to President Kenzaki.

348
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:00,861
Kanabun's resting at the hospital.

349
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:06,450
Always double-check
who you send invitations to.

350
00:22:06,950 --> 00:22:07,868
That girl,

351
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,871
she just had her stitches out.

352
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:12,831
My apologies.

353
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:15,334
The media can't know.

354
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:18,962
They haven't found anything out?

355
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:21,214
No.

356
00:22:26,386 --> 00:22:30,557
<i>Sales have been growing steadily</i>
<i>over the past month, but what concerns me</i>

357
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:31,725
is that the revenue gap

358
00:22:31,808 --> 00:22:34,686
between the Roppongi flagship
and our other locations

359
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:36,730
has widened since last year.

360
00:22:36,813 --> 00:22:39,399
Plus, the revenue gap
between the director and the other doctors

361
00:22:39,483 --> 00:22:40,942
is the largest it's ever been.

362
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:43,320
Does anyone have something to say?

363
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:47,407
I have one set of hands.

364
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:49,451
I only have one body.

365
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:53,288
If it's too hard
to get an appointment with us,

366
00:22:54,247 --> 00:22:56,375
then we might start losing patients.

367
00:22:57,667 --> 00:22:58,585
Um,

368
00:22:59,378 --> 00:23:00,504
I have a suggestion.

369
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:03,715
What if we ran an ad

370
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:07,052
positioning all our doctors
as successors of the Hand of God?

371
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:08,762
And why would we do that?

372
00:23:08,845 --> 00:23:12,641
The image of the chairman,
your predecessor, is still very strong,

373
00:23:13,141 --> 00:23:16,228
and a lot of clients associate
Tohyama Clinic with the Hand of God.

374
00:23:16,311 --> 00:23:17,396
SUCCESSOR OF THE HAND OF GOD

375
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:20,190
That's why all the bookings
are concentrated on you, Director.

376
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:21,441
The problem is…

377
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:24,861
…I think that would be
lying to our clients.

378
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:26,363
What?

379
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:31,326
It'd be strange
to have that many gods, wouldn't it?

380
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:36,790
That's right. I apologize.

381
00:23:38,834 --> 00:23:43,296
Well, as it happens, we've started
looking for highly-skilled doctors,

382
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:45,590
including those from general medicine.

383
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,884
- Takashina.
- Yes.

384
00:23:50,011 --> 00:23:54,391
Offering great skill at every scale,
big and small, that

385
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:57,144
is the value of Tohyama Clinic.

386
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:02,649
I expect everyone
to keep working to improve their skills.

387
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:05,569
In the event earnings fall,

388
00:24:05,652 --> 00:24:08,155
I won't hesitate to restaff doctors.

389
00:24:09,406 --> 00:24:10,699
Just remember that.

390
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:14,953
8. FUMI NUMATA
EMERGENCY/RECONSTRUCTIVE SURGERY

391
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:25,213
No, seriously, I feel a lot better.

392
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:27,257
Like a huge weight has been lifted.

393
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:29,885
Maybe it's because I was able
to sleep so well with the anesthesia.

394
00:24:29,968 --> 00:24:31,970
I actually feel better
than I did before I got sick.

395
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:33,805
<i>Well, good. I'm glad it wasn't worse.</i>

396
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:35,599
<i>Especially with the GC coming up.</i>

397
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,767
Oh, yeah, about that…

398
00:24:37,851 --> 00:24:40,312
- I thought of a cool thing to do.
- <i>What is it?</i>

399
00:24:40,395 --> 00:24:43,815
What if we start rolling the cameras
24 hours before the event?

400
00:24:43,899 --> 00:24:45,609
<i>Like a behind-the-scenes documentary?</i>

401
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:48,320
Exactly! Like those celebrity docs.

402
00:24:48,403 --> 00:24:49,654
I can see the banner.

403
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:51,656
"Kanabun's lifelong dream comes true."

404
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:54,242
"She's joining
the Girls Collection family."

405
00:24:56,703 --> 00:24:57,537
<i>Hm?</i>

406
00:24:58,622 --> 00:24:59,539
<i>What's wrong?</i>

407
00:25:00,749 --> 00:25:01,917
It's gone?

408
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:05,795
<i>Gone? What's gone?</i>

409
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:14,346
<i>What's wrong? Kana?</i>

410
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:19,809
What the…

411
00:25:23,021 --> 00:25:25,106
Where the hell did it go?!

412
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:30,904
How dare you make a decision like that?
What is wrong with you people?!

413
00:25:30,987 --> 00:25:34,574
We sincerely apologize.
The doctor said it was an emergency.

414
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:36,826
I told them
to leave the silicone in its place!

415
00:25:37,452 --> 00:25:38,495
Didn't I tell you?!

416
00:25:39,162 --> 00:25:42,582
- That, uh, was…
- The GC is in two weeks.

417
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:44,417
- I can't go like this!
- It's unacceptable!

418
00:25:44,501 --> 00:25:47,337
It's the Girls Collection.
Do you understand? Girls Collection!

419
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:51,007
Do you idiots know how hard she's worked
to appear at the GC?!

420
00:25:51,091 --> 00:25:52,592
We are truly sorry.

421
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:55,262
- Come on, Chief, stop apologizing.
- Huh?

422
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:56,221
Numata.

423
00:25:56,721 --> 00:25:58,765
This is a hospital.

424
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:01,351
We removed the source of her condition.

425
00:26:01,434 --> 00:26:03,979
Are you seriously willing
to risk your life for your looks?

426
00:26:04,062 --> 00:26:06,106
You promised the silicone would stay in.

427
00:26:06,189 --> 00:26:09,317
If we put it back in and you die,
the GC won't matter anyway.

428
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:11,027
Watch your mouth.
Who do you think you are?

429
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:14,447
Sir, please calm down.
And Dr. Numata, do watch your mouth.

430
00:26:17,284 --> 00:26:18,535
Here.

431
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:20,745
I'll kill myself.

432
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:25,125
Look, let me be clear.

433
00:26:25,625 --> 00:26:28,628
I had to take the silicone out
because you were in critical condition

434
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:29,921
and about to die.

435
00:26:30,005 --> 00:26:31,881
If I hadn't taken it out,
you might have died.

436
00:26:31,965 --> 00:26:33,675
What don't you get, you moron?

437
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:35,135
I want to die!

438
00:26:36,177 --> 00:26:37,095
Huh?

439
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:41,266
Hey, stop. Kanabun, calm down!

440
00:26:41,349 --> 00:26:43,184
Kanabun, easy, easy. Sit down.

441
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:06,708
SNACK BAR ITTENBARI

442
00:27:17,802 --> 00:27:19,471
I think we need another.

443
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:21,556
I'm back.

444
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,016
So early.

445
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:26,061
- What's going on, Fumi?
- I'm not feeling well.

446
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:29,356
You're not wearing makeup.
Did you go to work like that?

447
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:30,899
Oh, my, it's embarrassing.

448
00:27:30,982 --> 00:27:32,025
Leave me alone.

449
00:27:32,525 --> 00:27:34,944
Hey, no! Mama was saving that for later!

450
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:37,197
Hey, the seasoning's
really good this time.

451
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:38,865
- Did you add sugar?
- I can't believe this.

452
00:27:38,948 --> 00:27:42,327
Eat with us. Mr. Makihara,
could you boil up one more portion?

453
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:43,953
Sure thing.

454
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:45,955
How many bundles do you want?

455
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:52,462
Ah. I'm sorry
for calling during surgery last night.

456
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:57,092
You know what? I'm not that hungry.

457
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:13,525
Why is Nagomi Bank
boiling noodles in my house?!

458
00:28:13,608 --> 00:28:15,694
This is trespassing.
Did you call the cops?

459
00:28:16,319 --> 00:28:18,321
- Dad let him in.
- What?

460
00:28:18,405 --> 00:28:21,157
Dad says that modern loan sharks
don't use violence anymore.

461
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:24,494
They don't want to get sued. So you're
better off making them your allies.

462
00:28:24,994 --> 00:28:26,913
That's why you were having lunch together.

463
00:28:26,996 --> 00:28:28,957
- Yeah.
- What an idiot!

464
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,960
No wonder dad racked up
200 million yen in debt!

465
00:28:32,043 --> 00:28:34,629
But he doesn't seem like such a bad guy.

466
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:36,631
- Hmph.
- Here you go.

467
00:28:37,132 --> 00:28:38,383
What's that?

468
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:41,845
You left work early again after
getting chewed out by your boss, right?

469
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:47,308
Oh, Takeru!

470
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:50,687
You're the only one
who really understands me.

471
00:28:50,770 --> 00:28:54,524
I got in trouble today
only because I saved someone's life.

472
00:28:54,607 --> 00:28:55,942
How silly is that?

473
00:28:56,025 --> 00:29:00,739
I'm serious. Some folks you just
can't talk to. They're a lost cause.

474
00:29:00,822 --> 00:29:03,074
- And that's what I was trying to explain--
- Do you mind?

475
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:04,868
My fave's going live in a sec.

476
00:29:05,869 --> 00:29:06,786
- Your fave?
- Mm.

477
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,289
- Who is she, a K-pop girl?
- No, you wouldn't know her.

478
00:29:09,372 --> 00:29:10,832
Tell me…

479
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:12,584
- Hey, who is it?
- You don't know her.

480
00:29:12,667 --> 00:29:13,918
Try me. Who is she?

481
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:15,628
- A model.
- Mm-hmm.

482
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:16,755
A model.

483
00:29:17,338 --> 00:29:19,758
- Kanabun. She's amazing.
- Kanabun?

484
00:29:19,841 --> 00:29:20,842
Mm.

485
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:24,679
No, forget about her.
Stay away from that one. I'm not kidding.

486
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:26,723
- What? Kanabun?
- Mm.

487
00:29:26,806 --> 00:29:27,807
Wait, the one…

488
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:29,392
- She's cute.
- With the, uh…

489
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:31,394
- Cute, huh?
- Mm.

490
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:36,524
Okay, Ms. Tanaka. We're going to be
taking your photos in the studio today.

491
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:38,193
- Right.
- Yoshiko.

492
00:29:38,276 --> 00:29:40,111
Ah.

493
00:29:40,195 --> 00:29:41,237
You're back.

494
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,198
I'm glad. I knew I'd see you again.

495
00:29:45,992 --> 00:29:47,702
I requested the director.

496
00:29:48,203 --> 00:29:49,871
There was a cancellation,
so I squeezed in.

497
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:51,998
Oh.

498
00:29:53,583 --> 00:29:54,709
Hm.

499
00:29:55,376 --> 00:29:57,462
Eyes to the camera, please.

500
00:30:00,006 --> 00:30:01,090
Since I'm doing this,

501
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:03,051
I won't compromise.

502
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:09,349
I can make your eyes, nose and jaw
the way you want.

503
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:15,146
I think we should also shave the jawline
a little for overall balance.

504
00:30:16,606 --> 00:30:19,526
It'll give you a delicate
and sophisticated look.

505
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:21,319
So…?

506
00:30:22,737 --> 00:30:24,447
JAWLINE REDUCTION
¥1,520,000

507
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:28,368
Dr. Tohyama, whatever you say.
I'm in your hands.

508
00:30:28,451 --> 00:30:30,245
I appreciate that.

509
00:30:30,328 --> 00:30:34,374
But getting every surgery done
before the audition

510
00:30:34,874 --> 00:30:36,334
would be too hard on your body.

511
00:30:36,918 --> 00:30:39,295
So first, we'll do your eyes.

512
00:30:39,879 --> 00:30:42,632
Then we'll fix your nose and jawline.

513
00:30:43,675 --> 00:30:45,385
And we'll take care of your E-line.

514
00:30:45,885 --> 00:30:48,388
We'll make sure those are done
in time for your audition.

515
00:30:49,472 --> 00:30:50,473
It'll be okay.

516
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:53,268
Yes.

517
00:30:58,356 --> 00:31:00,900
- <i>You're really getting surgery</i>?
- Yeah.

518
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:04,571
I need to show that kind of commitment
if I want my parents on board.

519
00:31:05,196 --> 00:31:08,157
Oh, and about that drinking gig
you invited me to,

520
00:31:08,658 --> 00:31:09,701
I want to do it.

521
00:31:09,784 --> 00:31:12,662
I need to earn extra money. Can I join in?

522
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:25,133
I mean, isn't she an angel?

523
00:31:29,596 --> 00:31:30,680
What?

524
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:34,100
- It's confidential. I can't say.
- Come on.

525
00:31:35,810 --> 00:31:38,354
- Oh, she posted a story.
- What if I said it anyway?

526
00:31:38,855 --> 00:31:40,982
- I could give you a hint.
- Holy crap!

527
00:31:41,482 --> 00:31:42,609
What's wrong?

528
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:46,487
It says that Kanabun's dead.

529
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:47,655
What?!

530
00:31:52,827 --> 00:31:55,413
WE REGRET TO ANNOUNCE
THE PASSING OF KANA KOKUBUN

531
00:31:56,873 --> 00:31:58,166
Are you serious?

532
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:06,466
<i>I'll kill myself!</i>

533
00:32:12,722 --> 00:32:14,349
Disciplinary action?

534
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:16,517
A one-month suspension to start,

535
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:19,771
and after that, you'll be transferred
to an affiliated hospital.

536
00:32:19,854 --> 00:32:21,773
Wait a sec. Why am I being disciplined?

537
00:32:21,856 --> 00:32:23,274
Isn't it obvious?

538
00:32:23,358 --> 00:32:26,569
The patient explicitly asked
to be restored to her prior condition.

539
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:28,488
And you disregarded her request.

540
00:32:28,571 --> 00:32:30,323
Isn't that right, Tojo?

541
00:32:31,699 --> 00:32:35,703
And it appears that Ms. Kokubun
left a suicide note.

542
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:39,040
She wrote,
"I will never forgive Dr. Numata."

543
00:32:39,874 --> 00:32:41,417
No. I mean…

544
00:32:41,918 --> 00:32:43,962
She had a foreign object
lodged in her body

545
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:46,005
and she clearly was in critical condition.

546
00:32:46,089 --> 00:32:48,174
Isn't it a doctor's job
to save patients like that?

547
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:50,176
Am I wrong?

548
00:32:51,344 --> 00:32:54,847
Actually, if anyone's to blame,
it's the cosmetic surgeon.

549
00:32:54,931 --> 00:32:57,433
Performing a breast augmentation
on a patient with a tumor

550
00:32:57,517 --> 00:33:00,061
is a huge violation of medical ethics.

551
00:33:00,144 --> 00:33:04,232
First of all, there were many complaints
about your conduct already.

552
00:33:04,315 --> 00:33:07,568
You were taking breaks in
the inpatient ward without authorization.

553
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:11,781
And you made other staff
deal with your personal debt collectors.

554
00:33:12,281 --> 00:33:14,158
Isn't that right, Tojo?

555
00:33:15,284 --> 00:33:16,452
Good grief.

556
00:33:16,536 --> 00:33:19,789
You should be grateful
you still have a job.

557
00:33:21,749 --> 00:33:22,750
Then I'm out of here.

558
00:33:24,085 --> 00:33:25,962
- What?
- Numata?

559
00:33:27,255 --> 00:33:30,842
If this hospital won't support
its doctors, then I'd better quit.

560
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:34,804
Hey, uh, Numata, wait!

561
00:33:35,805 --> 00:33:38,391
<i>Her condition deteriorated</i>
<i>because of the silicone?</i>

562
00:33:39,767 --> 00:33:42,353
That's impossible.
Was that doctor qualified?

563
00:33:42,437 --> 00:33:44,814
I mean, I wouldn't
call that woman a doctor.

564
00:33:45,314 --> 00:33:46,691
She was out of her depth.

565
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,862
Poor Kanabun.
Sorry she had to go through that.

566
00:33:53,114 --> 00:33:55,742
Oh, I'm late.

567
00:33:56,242 --> 00:33:57,744
The trial ran long this morning.

568
00:33:57,827 --> 00:33:58,995
- Oh, Mr. Kenzaki.
- Hi.

569
00:33:59,078 --> 00:34:02,498
Hello. How far did you get?
I haven't had lunch. Mind if I eat?

570
00:34:07,253 --> 00:34:08,796
Hey, Numata.

571
00:34:09,839 --> 00:34:10,965
I'm sorry.

572
00:34:11,924 --> 00:34:14,135
I never thought
it would turn out like that.

573
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:16,137
I should have protected you.

574
00:34:16,637 --> 00:34:19,390
Don't act like my boyfriend
just because we slept together once.

575
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:23,144
I'm not interested in your sorries.
I won't go down without a fight.

576
00:34:23,227 --> 00:34:24,479
Hey…

577
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:33,905
- Mr. Inoue, I need your help.
- Mm-hmm.

578
00:34:33,988 --> 00:34:38,076
I will not be satisfied
until I see that quack behind bars.

579
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:41,621
If that's what you want,
I can't exactly say no, can I?

580
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:44,373
But that means
Kanabun's surgery will be exposed.

581
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:48,086
- Huh?
- What do you expect?

582
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,295
If this goes to court,

583
00:34:49,378 --> 00:34:53,007
the whole case hinges on whether
it was necessary to remove the implant.

584
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:57,053
And the second that comes up, there'll be
questions about the other models as well.

585
00:34:57,136 --> 00:34:58,387
You sure your agency wants that?

586
00:34:58,471 --> 00:35:00,389
Yeah. Uh, no…

587
00:35:00,473 --> 00:35:03,059
In other words,
I think the risk is too high.

588
00:35:03,142 --> 00:35:04,811
And on top of that…

589
00:35:04,894 --> 00:35:08,064
…the doctor may try
to shift the blame onto you,

590
00:35:08,147 --> 00:35:09,816
so we need to get ahead of that.

591
00:35:09,899 --> 00:35:11,400
No, wait, hold on.

592
00:35:11,484 --> 00:35:13,653
Why are we the ones
who have to deal with that?

593
00:35:13,736 --> 00:35:16,447
Because no one
wants to be labeled a murderer.

594
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:20,284
She'll argue the procedure
was 100% necessary to save her life.

595
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:24,831
That the blame should fall on whoever
put an implant in a breast with a tumor.

596
00:35:29,418 --> 00:35:31,420
I'll get straight to the point.

597
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:33,965
Is there any way
to stop her from filing charges?

598
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:38,052
Absolutely not.

599
00:35:38,136 --> 00:35:40,847
That is a right everyone's entitled to.

600
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,141
But, still,

601
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:47,061
we might be able
to weaken the credibility of the charges.

602
00:35:48,604 --> 00:35:50,398
And for that, oh…

603
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:55,611
we'll need Mr. Takashina's help.

604
00:36:04,912 --> 00:36:07,957
- Mr. Takashi!
- Whoo! Yeah!

605
00:36:10,751 --> 00:36:12,253
Come on, let's dance!

606
00:36:12,336 --> 00:36:14,130
Whoo!

607
00:36:15,089 --> 00:36:16,090
Whoo!

608
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:23,681
STILL NOT OVER KANABUN.
DROP THE SURGERY TALK

609
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:25,474
KANABUN NEVER HAD PLASTIC SURGERY

610
00:36:25,558 --> 00:36:26,767
PLASTIC SURGERY? WHERE?

611
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:29,061
Even the comments are fake.

612
00:36:29,145 --> 00:36:31,606
Excuse me. I brought you some tea.

613
00:36:31,689 --> 00:36:33,232
You can't just walk in!

614
00:36:33,941 --> 00:36:34,775
So sorry.

615
00:36:37,737 --> 00:36:41,574
Well, then, I'll just leave it here.

616
00:36:46,662 --> 00:36:48,331
Plastic surgery, huh?

617
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:52,627
- You're switching to plastic surgery?
- Of course not, moron.

618
00:36:53,836 --> 00:36:55,421
I hear it pays really well.

619
00:36:55,504 --> 00:36:57,506
Might make it easier
to take care of your debt.

620
00:36:57,590 --> 00:37:00,885
Listen. I'm not blood-related
to that old guy downstairs.

621
00:37:00,968 --> 00:37:04,055
He's just my mother's new husband.
All right? We're total strangers.

622
00:37:04,138 --> 00:37:05,181
Just a reminder,

623
00:37:05,264 --> 00:37:08,893
if the transfer doesn't clear by tomorrow,
then the interest rate will be--

624
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:11,479
Shut up and get out now!

625
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:13,272
Out. Out!

626
00:37:13,356 --> 00:37:15,316
The interest rate…

627
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:22,156
STILL NOT OVER KANABUN

628
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:24,700
SHE LOOKS NOTHING LIKE SHE DID
AS A KID. THERE'S PROOF

629
00:37:29,705 --> 00:37:31,415
SURGERY DISASTERS OKURA

630
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:35,544
EXPOSING THE DARK SIDE AND DISASTERS
OF THE COSMETIC SURGERY INDUSTRY

631
00:37:38,798 --> 00:37:42,134
No, seriously, Tanaka's voice is insane.

632
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:44,387
Hey, Tanaka, do Nastassia.

633
00:37:44,470 --> 00:37:46,013
She sounds exactly like her!

634
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:49,267
Really? Do it, please.
My daughter's obsessed with this show.

635
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:52,561
Okay, could you close your eyes?

636
00:37:53,437 --> 00:37:54,355
Just for a sec.

637
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:02,029
"Every last one of you,
you're a bunch of pigs."

638
00:38:03,864 --> 00:38:08,035
"Greedy little piggies like you
should be happy to lick my feet."

639
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:10,913
- That sounded just like her!
- Right?

640
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:13,207
Like she was here.

641
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:14,542
She's really good.

642
00:38:16,794 --> 00:38:22,842
COSMETIC SURGERY CREMATORIUM:
SURGERY DISASTERS OKURA

643
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:25,011
I BET IT'S THE T-YAMA DIRECTOR
I'VE RUN INTO HER

644
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:26,762
T-yama?

645
00:38:31,183 --> 00:38:33,519
T-YAMA COSMETIC CLINIC

646
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:36,272
TOHYAMA COSMETIC SURGERY CLINIC

647
00:38:36,939 --> 00:38:39,150
TOHYAMA
REBIRTH

648
00:38:44,864 --> 00:38:46,490
SUCCESSOR OF THE HAND OF GOD

649
00:38:47,408 --> 00:38:48,534
<i>Tanaka,</i>

650
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:50,661
do you have any plans right now, or…

651
00:38:51,454 --> 00:38:52,538
Not really, no.

652
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:53,497
Oh.

653
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:58,294
I think you've caught the eye
of the chubby one.

654
00:39:03,382 --> 00:39:04,675
He said he'd give you

655
00:39:05,259 --> 00:39:06,510
this for a date.

656
00:39:10,264 --> 00:39:12,475
<i>This audition will be decided by looks.</i>

657
00:39:12,558 --> 00:39:13,809
We'll get through this.

658
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:23,319
I KNOW HOW KANABUN REALLY DIED.
CAN WE MEET IN PERSON?

659
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:39,418
Oh, wait, wait, wait. Wait a minute!

660
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:43,464
- I said no kissing, remember?
- Oh, yeah. Sorry.

661
00:39:44,173 --> 00:39:47,134
Hey, can you
do the Nastassia voice though?

662
00:39:47,635 --> 00:39:48,636
Come on. Please?

663
00:40:00,773 --> 00:40:02,525
MOM

664
00:40:33,264 --> 00:40:34,265
It's okay.

665
00:40:36,350 --> 00:40:38,144
Let's trust Dr. Rin.

666
00:40:42,148 --> 00:40:44,275
Excuse me, Ms. Tanaka.

667
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:49,989
Everything's ready for you, okay?
We can start.

668
00:40:51,574 --> 00:40:52,450
Okay.

669
00:40:55,786 --> 00:40:58,539
- This is from yesterday.
- I saw it. It's crazy!

670
00:40:58,622 --> 00:40:59,957
So good-looking.

671
00:41:08,841 --> 00:41:10,134
Excuse me…

672
00:41:10,926 --> 00:41:12,553
Are you the one who reached out?

673
00:41:12,636 --> 00:41:15,347
Oh, are you Okura?

674
00:41:15,931 --> 00:41:18,225
Yeah. I'm Okura.

675
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:20,394
Nice to meet you.

676
00:41:21,812 --> 00:41:22,813
Wanna sit somewhere?

677
00:41:22,897 --> 00:41:23,939
Sounds good.

678
00:41:26,025 --> 00:41:27,067
This is Okayu.

679
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,819
Oh. Ah.

680
00:41:31,906 --> 00:41:35,451
Fans think Kanabun's plastic surgery
was an open secret.

681
00:41:35,534 --> 00:41:39,079
Actually, every model at the agency
has had work done.

682
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,081
Was hers done at Tohyama Clinic?

683
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,082
Yeah.

684
00:41:42,583 --> 00:41:46,253
They say it was handled by the director.

685
00:41:47,129 --> 00:41:48,297
Is, um,

686
00:41:48,797 --> 00:41:51,425
Kanabun's death connected
to Tohyama Clinic too?

687
00:41:55,721 --> 00:41:57,890
Yeah? Whoa!

688
00:42:02,144 --> 00:42:03,145
Well, then,

689
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:05,981
it's time to say goodbye

690
00:42:06,690 --> 00:42:07,900
to your current self.

691
00:42:23,332 --> 00:42:24,208
Okay.

692
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:27,503
Okay, I'm ready.

693
00:42:30,923 --> 00:42:32,216
Do you trust me?

694
00:42:33,133 --> 00:42:33,968
Yes.

695
00:42:47,064 --> 00:42:49,608
Okay, this might sting a little.
Here we go.

696
00:42:53,445 --> 00:42:57,533
- Tohyama, huh? That's a tough one.
- Why is that?

697
00:42:57,616 --> 00:43:02,329
Huh. It's like the director
is basically a celebrity at this point.

698
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:06,917
<i>Her father's famous, too,</i>
<i>and they advertise everywhere.</i>

699
00:43:07,418 --> 00:43:11,171
<i>The media will ignore it</i>
<i>unless there's overwhelming evidence.</i>

700
00:43:11,255 --> 00:43:13,007
Well, actually, I've got some.

701
00:43:13,841 --> 00:43:15,426
Before she passed away,

702
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:19,471
Ms. Kanabun had an emergency surgery
and I know the surgeon very well.

703
00:43:19,555 --> 00:43:22,391
Will that surgeon
agree to talk on camera or not?

704
00:43:22,474 --> 00:43:23,726
On camera?

705
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:28,397
Well, no, sorry. Um…

706
00:43:29,023 --> 00:43:30,232
As a matter of fact,

707
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:33,402
Tohyama Clinic is very well-protected,
so you know.

708
00:43:34,111 --> 00:43:36,196
<i>And their lawyers are ruthless.</i>

709
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:39,533
<i>I heard they even hired</i>
<i>a former detective for crisis management.</i>

710
00:43:40,242 --> 00:43:41,327
Really?

711
00:43:42,745 --> 00:43:44,872
Oh, going out, Mr. Makihara?

712
00:43:45,748 --> 00:43:47,750
Going to collect from another client.

713
00:43:47,833 --> 00:43:48,876
Ah.

714
00:43:48,959 --> 00:43:51,253
Oh, by the way,
the prep for dinner's all done.

715
00:43:51,337 --> 00:43:53,213
- Oh, thank you, as always.
- Oh, no, no.

716
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:55,466
Mr. Makihara, why don't you
just move in with us?

717
00:43:55,549 --> 00:43:58,802
What?

718
00:43:58,886 --> 00:44:01,138
- Okay, see you later.
- Take care.

719
00:44:06,477 --> 00:44:08,103
Are you with Nagomi Bank?

720
00:44:12,149 --> 00:44:14,360
Huh? Can I help you?

721
00:44:14,443 --> 00:44:17,571
I would like to talk to you
about the Numata family's debt.

722
00:44:20,991 --> 00:44:22,868
- Huh? What--
- In the car!

723
00:44:22,951 --> 00:44:24,203
What the hell?

724
00:44:24,286 --> 00:44:27,873
Do you know of any other third party
who might be willing to testify?

725
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:31,085
I don't think I do.

726
00:44:31,168 --> 00:44:33,420
If the surgeon won't go on record,

727
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:35,964
we'll need multiple testimonies.

728
00:44:36,048 --> 00:44:37,883
For example, someone

729
00:44:38,967 --> 00:44:41,428
who was actually at the party
when she got sick.

730
00:44:45,557 --> 00:44:46,392
Wait.

731
00:44:46,475 --> 00:44:50,062
Yeah. She got a few shots and then
she just started drifting in and out.

732
00:44:58,529 --> 00:45:00,739
<i>Oh, you mean Ms. Tanaka.</i>

733
00:45:00,823 --> 00:45:05,786
Yes. I wanted to thank her for bringing
the patient to the ER that night.

734
00:45:07,413 --> 00:45:08,622
Hey, Hina,

735
00:45:08,706 --> 00:45:09,915
is Ms. Tanaka here yet?

736
00:45:09,998 --> 00:45:12,376
Uh, no. Ms. Tanaka's off today.

737
00:45:12,459 --> 00:45:16,922
Uh… I really need to talk to her soon.
Her next shift, when is it?

738
00:45:17,506 --> 00:45:20,968
I don't know when she'll be here again.

739
00:45:21,051 --> 00:45:23,137
I heard she's taking two weeks off.

740
00:45:23,220 --> 00:45:25,222
- Two weeks off?
- At least.

741
00:45:25,723 --> 00:45:27,516
Ah, no. Uh…

742
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:30,936
Maybe I could reach out to her directly?

743
00:46:05,804 --> 00:46:07,431
There's still some swelling,

744
00:46:07,514 --> 00:46:10,225
so you might be startled
when you see yourself.

745
00:46:11,059 --> 00:46:12,352
But rest assured,

746
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,773
it went really well.

747
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:26,784
Try to stay home for the next
two weeks until the swelling goes down.

748
00:46:27,367 --> 00:46:29,077
Eat well and take it easy.

749
00:46:29,161 --> 00:46:30,913
Once you get through that,

750
00:46:32,289 --> 00:46:36,627
you'll become a whole new person,
Ms. Tanaka.

751
00:46:39,880 --> 00:46:40,964
Recovery time

752
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:44,092
is what's necessary
for a chrysalis to break out of its cocoon

753
00:46:44,176 --> 00:46:46,762
and transform into a butterfly.

754
00:46:47,721 --> 00:46:49,056
OUR APPROACH TO RECOVERY TIME

755
00:46:49,139 --> 00:46:52,059
It might feel lonely, frightening even,

756
00:46:52,559 --> 00:46:54,853
to stay still in a dark cocoon.

757
00:46:56,355 --> 00:47:00,901
But when you want to fly
with beautiful wings,

758
00:47:02,277 --> 00:47:03,779
it's the price to pay.

759
00:47:05,781 --> 00:47:07,115
Hang in there.

760
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:08,534
You'll be okay.

761
00:47:27,219 --> 00:47:30,013
Oh, and I forgot to mention,

762
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:32,766
try not to cry if you can,

763
00:47:33,809 --> 00:47:35,727
or the swelling takes longer to heal.

764
00:47:38,355 --> 00:47:40,399
I wish you'd said so earlier.

765
00:47:40,482 --> 00:47:42,234
Mm.

766
00:47:51,076 --> 00:47:52,494
Sup? I'm back.

767
00:47:54,413 --> 00:47:56,707
What's going on?

768
00:47:57,791 --> 00:47:58,959
Fumi,

769
00:48:00,127 --> 00:48:01,670
why did you quit the hospital?

770
00:48:01,753 --> 00:48:02,796
Huh?

771
00:48:03,755 --> 00:48:07,593
I, uh… That hospital's so toxic.
You wouldn't believe all the drama there.

772
00:48:07,676 --> 00:48:09,845
Wait. How do you know?

773
00:48:11,221 --> 00:48:12,848
Ah, she's back.

774
00:48:15,392 --> 00:48:17,102
Okay, take a seat.

775
00:48:17,185 --> 00:48:19,980
- Huh? Why? I've got things to do.
- I said sit down!

776
00:48:23,275 --> 00:48:24,109
Go.

777
00:48:25,736 --> 00:48:26,737
Go!

778
00:48:31,199 --> 00:48:36,204
There are gonna be consequences
if you quit working as a doctor.

779
00:48:36,288 --> 00:48:37,289
Huh?

780
00:48:37,789 --> 00:48:40,250
Your salary is collateral on your debt.

781
00:48:40,334 --> 00:48:44,379
Of course it is. Did you think this
snack bar was gonna cover 200 million yen?

782
00:48:44,463 --> 00:48:48,383
I quit the hospital, but that doesn't mean
I quit being a doctor, okay?

783
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:52,471
Yeah, sure. But how are you
gonna get a job after that scandal?

784
00:48:53,055 --> 00:48:54,014
What scandal?

785
00:48:55,223 --> 00:48:56,266
Huh?

786
00:48:57,184 --> 00:48:58,268
God, you're clueless.

787
00:49:10,030 --> 00:49:11,031
What does it say?

788
00:49:11,114 --> 00:49:14,993
#FUMI_NUMATA #PSYCHO_DOCTOR
#MEDICAL_LICENSE_REVOKED

789
00:49:17,454 --> 00:49:19,039
What? What is this?

790
00:49:26,630 --> 00:49:29,883
- Yeah, hello?
- Hey, is everything okay over there?

791
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:33,095
The hospital is being swarmed
by the media.

792
00:49:33,178 --> 00:49:35,222
How is it
my personal information is out there?

793
00:49:37,224 --> 00:49:38,934
I've got no idea either.

794
00:49:39,726 --> 00:49:41,561
Hey, listen.
The chief wants to talk again.

795
00:49:43,355 --> 00:49:45,691
They'll want you
to give an official explanation.

796
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:49,861
Hello? Numata? You there?

797
00:49:50,612 --> 00:49:52,906
So, what do I do?

798
00:49:55,575 --> 00:49:57,744
Selling the house
would only clear 50 million yen, right?

799
00:50:01,915 --> 00:50:03,875
Hold on, Mr. Makihara.

800
00:50:06,253 --> 00:50:08,046
We'll figure it out. We will.

801
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:10,882
We'll keep this bar going
and pay you back little by little.

802
00:50:10,966 --> 00:50:12,467
Just don't take the house.

803
00:50:12,551 --> 00:50:14,011
Please. I beg you!

804
00:50:16,513 --> 00:50:20,559
Listen, my son, is still in junior high.

805
00:50:20,642 --> 00:50:22,519
Just, please, give…

806
00:50:23,103 --> 00:50:26,314
Just until he starts high school.
That's all I'm asking. Okay?

807
00:50:26,398 --> 00:50:27,941
Please. I beg you.

808
00:50:28,025 --> 00:50:29,860
Please. Until high school. That's all.

809
00:50:30,819 --> 00:50:32,237
Mr. Makihara.

810
00:50:33,071 --> 00:50:35,699
Th… This is all my fault.
I made bad investments.

811
00:50:35,782 --> 00:50:37,159
I'm such an idiot!

812
00:50:38,535 --> 00:50:42,456
I'll work as hard as I have to work.
I beg you!

813
00:50:45,751 --> 00:50:47,836
Mr. Makihara, please.

814
00:50:47,919 --> 00:50:48,920
Takeru.

815
00:50:58,096 --> 00:51:00,891
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

816
00:51:00,974 --> 00:51:03,810
Even if you beg, it doesn't change
the fact that you owe me money!

817
00:51:03,894 --> 00:51:04,895
I just need one more week.

818
00:51:05,687 --> 00:51:06,563
Huh?

819
00:51:07,689 --> 00:51:08,940
Takeru.

820
00:51:10,025 --> 00:51:12,027
Takeru, that's enough.

821
00:51:12,527 --> 00:51:13,361
I'm sorry.

822
00:51:13,445 --> 00:51:16,531
So, you're gonna get
200 million yen in a week?

823
00:51:16,615 --> 00:51:19,743
No, of course I won't.
But that scandal is based on lies.

824
00:51:19,826 --> 00:51:21,745
I'll set the record straight
and go back to work.

825
00:51:21,828 --> 00:51:24,247
As long as I'm working as a doctor,
we're good, right?

826
00:51:26,374 --> 00:51:27,751
Huh.

827
00:51:28,251 --> 00:51:29,503
That works for me.

828
00:51:30,087 --> 00:51:31,505
In one week then.

829
00:51:34,883 --> 00:51:37,552
Takeru. It's okay.

830
00:51:38,720 --> 00:51:39,805
I'm sorry.

831
00:51:40,305 --> 00:51:41,515
I'm sorry.

832
00:51:58,365 --> 00:52:00,742
Ms. Tanaka? Excuse me?

833
00:52:03,620 --> 00:52:04,746
Excuse-- Oh.

834
00:52:09,459 --> 00:52:10,460
Who is it?

835
00:52:10,544 --> 00:52:13,630
I'm Numata. We met
at Katsushika University Hospital.

836
00:52:13,713 --> 00:52:16,299
Um, I'm the one
who operated on Ms. Kanabun.

837
00:52:16,800 --> 00:52:17,801
What do you want?

838
00:52:18,760 --> 00:52:21,680
I need your help with something.
If you could give me a minute--

839
00:52:26,059 --> 00:52:26,977
Oh boy.

840
00:52:27,060 --> 00:52:29,729
I can't be associated
with a psycho doctor.

841
00:52:31,231 --> 00:52:33,358
- Just leave me alone.
- I just need a minute!

842
00:52:35,235 --> 00:52:36,319
Ms. Tanaka.

843
00:52:37,654 --> 00:52:38,738
Ms. Tanaka.

844
00:52:39,239 --> 00:52:40,866
I promise it won't take long at all.

845
00:52:42,075 --> 00:52:47,122
And now you've moved on to a new phase
involving debt evasion or something.

846
00:52:47,873 --> 00:52:50,041
Honestly, with so much heat,

847
00:52:50,125 --> 00:52:53,420
even my site can't help you on this one.

848
00:52:53,503 --> 00:52:54,546
All right.

849
00:52:55,255 --> 00:52:57,757
I'll go ahead
and share everything I know on camera.

850
00:52:57,841 --> 00:53:00,677
I'll talk about Kanabun's surgery
in details. Does that change things?

851
00:53:01,428 --> 00:53:02,846
- I'm sorry.
- Why?

852
00:53:02,929 --> 00:53:07,225
I mean, like I told you already,
Tohyama's bad news.

853
00:53:07,726 --> 00:53:10,645
These people will seriously
stop at nothing.

854
00:53:11,646 --> 00:53:12,480
What?

855
00:53:13,315 --> 00:53:16,735
So Tohyama is behind the scandal?

856
00:53:17,360 --> 00:53:18,820
I think it's very likely.

857
00:53:19,529 --> 00:53:21,573
That's… That's too far.

858
00:53:21,656 --> 00:53:25,619
I mean, a company that runs commercials
on TV wouldn't act like a bunch of yakuza.

859
00:53:25,702 --> 00:53:28,121
That's the plastic surgery industry
for you.

860
00:53:30,624 --> 00:53:33,335
Since reviews have an effect on sales,

861
00:53:33,835 --> 00:53:37,756
they get rid of negative publicity
by any means necessary.

862
00:53:37,839 --> 00:53:41,134
Business owners, and celebrities…

863
00:53:41,635 --> 00:53:44,429
They have close ties
with influential people.

864
00:53:45,055 --> 00:53:46,890
So their misdeeds are covered up,

865
00:53:46,973 --> 00:53:50,435
and there are a lot of citizens
who are frustrated.

866
00:53:50,936 --> 00:53:53,438
Which is why my site is so successful.

867
00:53:57,442 --> 00:53:59,945
ARE YOU SATISFIED WITH WHO YOU ARE NOW?

868
00:54:06,201 --> 00:54:09,955
So today we're at the top-rated
plastic surgery clinic,

869
00:54:10,038 --> 00:54:11,665
Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic.

870
00:54:11,748 --> 00:54:12,874
- Isn't it exciting?
- Thanks.

871
00:54:12,958 --> 00:54:14,417
- Thank you.
- We're finally here.

872
00:54:14,501 --> 00:54:15,710
- This is amazing.
- Yeah.

873
00:54:15,794 --> 00:54:18,255
Okay, without further ado, here they are.

874
00:54:18,338 --> 00:54:19,881
Oh, wonderful!

875
00:54:19,965 --> 00:54:22,384
- Wow! Incredible. This is the director.
- Wow!

876
00:54:22,467 --> 00:54:23,927
- Thanks for having us.
- Hello.

877
00:54:24,010 --> 00:54:26,888
Wow, the Hand of God
has an intense aura, doesn't she?

878
00:54:26,972 --> 00:54:27,806
What a treat.

879
00:54:27,889 --> 00:54:29,432
I know this is a weird question to ask,

880
00:54:29,516 --> 00:54:31,643
but how much would it cost
to get a facelift like yours?

881
00:54:31,726 --> 00:54:33,395
- That's rude!
- Oh, I'm so sorry.

882
00:54:33,478 --> 00:54:35,480
I actually haven't had
any work done myself yet.

883
00:54:35,563 --> 00:54:36,898
- Really?
- Really?

884
00:54:37,565 --> 00:54:38,608
This is unadulterated?

885
00:54:38,692 --> 00:54:41,569
"Unadulterated?"
I don't think that's how it's called.

886
00:54:41,653 --> 00:54:43,530
- Oh.
- You're so perfect.

887
00:54:43,613 --> 00:54:44,864
Hey--

888
00:54:44,948 --> 00:54:46,574
Do you have an appointment?

889
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:47,659
I need to talk to you.

890
00:54:47,742 --> 00:54:49,494
- Can I help you?
- What's going on?

891
00:54:49,577 --> 00:54:51,955
You know why I'm here.
This is about Ms. Kanabun.

892
00:54:52,038 --> 00:54:54,332
We can schedule you
for a consultation later?

893
00:54:54,416 --> 00:54:56,960
- I just want to have a word.
- Ma'am, you need to stop.

894
00:54:58,878 --> 00:55:02,549
And you call yourself a doctor? Huh?

895
00:55:03,508 --> 00:55:06,344
How can you live with yourself
after a surgery like that?!

896
00:55:06,428 --> 00:55:07,762
- Stop, now!
- Hey!

897
00:55:11,975 --> 00:55:16,438
What kind of beauty is that? Screw you!
It was you. You killed that girl!

898
00:55:16,521 --> 00:55:18,523
- This way.
- Go to hell!

899
00:55:18,606 --> 00:55:19,941
- Come on.
- Let go of me!

900
00:55:20,025 --> 00:55:22,068
- Come on.
- Hey, you!

901
00:55:22,152 --> 00:55:24,070
Hey!

902
00:55:24,988 --> 00:55:28,325
Stop it! Enough!

903
00:55:30,368 --> 00:55:33,872
Ha. God, that went exactly as expected.

904
00:55:34,372 --> 00:55:35,999
Actually, better than expected.

905
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:39,252
Now you don't have to worry
about any allegations.

906
00:55:39,794 --> 00:55:41,713
You don't know her.

907
00:55:50,263 --> 00:55:53,016
I don't think she'll give up that easily.

908
00:55:55,852 --> 00:55:59,147
- We need to find a way to stop that girl.
- It's already taken care of.

909
00:55:59,647 --> 00:56:03,526
The university hospital just put out a
statement acknowledging the medical error.

910
00:56:03,610 --> 00:56:05,987
Whatever she says now,
nobody's gonna believe her.

911
00:56:06,071 --> 00:56:07,864
Ah, by the way,

912
00:56:08,365 --> 00:56:10,909
Mr. Takashina mentioned
something interesting.

913
00:56:10,992 --> 00:56:14,621
Do you remember that list
of top doctors we wanted to recruit?

914
00:56:16,790 --> 00:56:18,958
Well, there is someone.

915
00:56:20,251 --> 00:56:21,252
Here, look at this.

916
00:56:23,630 --> 00:56:24,964
It's that psycho doctor.

917
00:56:25,465 --> 00:56:26,591
FUMI NUMATA

918
00:56:28,176 --> 00:56:29,386
GRADE A

919
00:56:29,469 --> 00:56:31,179
She's got the highest technical score.

920
00:56:31,262 --> 00:56:32,389
She's pretty good.

921
00:56:45,902 --> 00:56:49,197
KITA-AZABU POLICE STATION

922
00:56:53,952 --> 00:56:54,911
Mm.

923
00:57:17,934 --> 00:57:19,310
Oh yeah. Yeah, yeah.

924
00:57:19,394 --> 00:57:21,646
Yeah. It was so much quicker
than the other ones.

925
00:57:37,078 --> 00:57:39,539
TOHYAMA
SUCCESSOR OF THE HAND OF GOD

926
00:58:19,829 --> 00:58:23,374
How would you like to work
at our cosmetic clinic?

927
00:58:24,876 --> 00:58:26,252
Huh? What are you saying?

928
00:58:28,922 --> 00:58:31,883
Don't take this the wrong way, Fumi,

929
00:58:32,800 --> 00:58:36,971
but I can guarantee you more than three
times your university hospital salary.

930
00:58:37,055 --> 00:58:38,806
Are you trying to buy my silence?

931
00:58:38,890 --> 00:58:39,974
How dirty are you?

932
00:58:41,601 --> 00:58:42,560
Dirty?

933
00:58:44,437 --> 00:58:45,563
Nothing dirty about this.

934
00:58:46,606 --> 00:58:50,693
I'm simply telling you, you would have
a nice, but fair salary, Doctor.

935
00:58:50,777 --> 00:58:54,072
Why would I ever
want to work in cosmetic surgery?

936
00:58:54,155 --> 00:58:56,115
We could take care of your debt as well.

937
00:58:56,616 --> 00:58:58,201
Two hundred million yen, wasn't it?

938
00:59:03,331 --> 00:59:05,625
I don't think it's such a bad deal.

939
00:59:09,087 --> 00:59:11,923
You can continue to practice medicine
like you always have.

940
00:59:13,383 --> 00:59:15,927
And you get to rescue your dear family.

941
00:59:26,271 --> 00:59:27,730
You're a bit curious.

942
00:59:28,356 --> 00:59:29,774
I'm right, aren't I?

943
00:59:37,282 --> 00:59:38,241
Hm.

944
00:59:45,582 --> 00:59:46,583
I won't forgive you.

945
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:49,752
- Sorry?
- I'll say it again.

946
00:59:50,545 --> 00:59:53,006
I… will never forgive you.

947
00:59:55,341 --> 00:59:57,885
I couldn't care less
if you forgive me or not.

948
00:59:58,511 --> 01:00:00,054
I care about one thing.

949
01:00:01,598 --> 01:00:04,726
I don't want the clinic's reputation
to be tarnished.

950
01:00:10,523 --> 01:00:11,399
Well, then,

951
01:00:12,108 --> 01:00:13,735
I'll wait for you at the clinic.

952
01:00:18,406 --> 01:00:19,449
Hey!

953
01:00:19,949 --> 01:00:20,825
Hey!

954
01:00:22,327 --> 01:00:25,204
Wait! Hey, go to hell!

955
01:00:25,705 --> 01:00:26,539
Okay?!

956
01:00:28,374 --> 01:00:29,751
Screw you!

957
01:01:04,994 --> 01:01:06,412
Go to hell!

958
01:01:13,002 --> 01:01:14,337
Go to hell!

959
01:01:23,596 --> 01:01:24,472
Shit!
